Builds the node's state once, before the framework opens any topic. The body takes it by
reference — `&mut S`, or `&S` for a state it only reads — and it is the one parameter
with no marker, wherever that stands in the list.

Limit: the state is not dropped when the framework ends the node. A failed start and a
`Fault` stop both end in `process::exit(1)`, so a `Drop` on `Motors` that stops the motors
does not run then. A device's safe state cannot rest on `Drop` (TAIL-437).

