The link spells the path because `robot_topics.rs` does not import the frames: an import
used only by a doc link is an unused import to the compiler, which `#![deny(warnings)]`
refuses. Each program includes both files by `#[path]`, so `crate::robot_frames` is the
same module in every program. The link is a reading aid, which rustdoc renders: nothing
checks that a node converts a topic's readings through the right frame.

