`lookup(target, source)` returns `T_target_source`, the transform that takes coordinates in
`source` to coordinates in `target`; the target comes first, as in the transform's
name. It walks both frames up the tree to where they meet and
composes the links it crosses: at most N - 1 of an N-frame set, with no allocation, no lock
and no clock. A lookup between frames joined by mounts always succeeds, and
`range.get()?.point()?` is `None` when the reading is absent, stale, or not a measured
distance. For the 4.2 m reading (an `f32`) the obstacle is at (4.156888286178356,
1.087039940064772, 0) in `base_link`: 4.2967 m away, 14.65 degrees to the left.

